  "applicability": {
    "goal_shape": "an identity f n = g n between two sequence-valued functions int -> rat that both satisfy the same first-order recurrence Urec and agree at one initial value (here n = 2)",
    "use_when": "the two sides of the identity obey the same recurrence and share an initial value, so one general 'same recurrence and same start imply equal' lemma settles the identity and the per-side recurrences become separate leaves",
    "avoid_when": "the two sides do not share a recurrence, or their initial values differ; the recurrence is of higher order, so the uniqueness induction and its coefficient-nonvanishing side conditions grow; one side's recurrence cannot be stated without the other's"
  },
